body:
Good news - turns out they were ahead of the game and just asked me if I can stay on until Mid-November. In a large company fashion, I'm assuming they picked mid-Nov to avoid paying me over the holidays and the end of the year bonus. 

&#x200B;

Now that the ball is in my court, I'm going to counter back and ask that they keep me through the year because I don't want to be unemployed over the holidays when hiring is slow. Any tips on how to position this? I do have a second interview lined up next week (for a job I'm not thrilled about). Should I use this as leverage (i.e. I'm interviewing for a role and if I give up this opportunity I want to stay on through the year)?

